# m3_loop: m3_boss's run carried on into the next stage (the sweep continued to 4299). Until
# M7 one table looped and this pinned the stage-2 beetle's crate; since M7 a clear moves on to
# the next of four stages, so it pins stage 2 (INTEGRATION) starting after the Heisenbug's
# clear (3338) and the 120-tick breather: its table starts at 3458 (phase 0) and its first
# entry, a centipede (head + 5 segments, 14 ticks apart) opened as a formation, enters at
# 3578, when the stage pop ends (the catch-up clock only runs after the pop). The A4 sweep
# shoots down every part of it; the last segment at 3696 completes the formation: crate 10
# drops (drops 9 -> 10) and +200 on top of the segment's 20 (score 4008 -> 4228). Crate 10 is
# the cores crate of the sequence; the sweep collects it at 3915 (cores 1 -> 2, +100).
# Re-pinned for the catch-up clock: stage 1 dropped more crates before the warp, so the
# formation's crate moved from the RETRY (crate 6, shield 0 -> 1 at 4208) to the cores crate
# (the shield came from crate 6 in stage 1, at 1687); the clear moved from 3662 to 3338.
--frames 4300 --call-at "31 debug_god" --call-at "1700 debug_warp" --dump-exports debug_state,debug_stage_index,debug_phase,debug_enemies,debug_shield --at "3457 debug_phase == 3" --at "3458 debug_phase == 0" --at "3458 debug_stage_index == 1" --at "3577 debug_enemies == 0" --at "3578 debug_enemies == 1" --at "3695 debug_drops == 9" --at "3695 debug_score == 4008" --at "3696 debug_drops == 10" --at "3696 debug_score == 4228" --at "3696 debug_pickups == 1" --at "3914 debug_cores == 1" --at "3915 debug_cores == 2" --at "3915 debug_pickups == 0" --at "3915 debug_shield == 1" --at "4000 debug_history_check == 0" --at "4299 debug_history_check == 0" --expect "debug_stage_index == 1" --expect "debug_state == 1"
